      "created_at": "2016-01-02T01:13:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I really, really feel I should know this, but here goes. If a card refers to a value of X, where X = (insert explanation here), can X ever change in the middle of resolution of damage, or is it a set number until all damage is dealt?</p><p><span>For example (the scenario which actually prompted this quesiton), The Dreamer's Night Terrors was played. There were two explosives wagons in play. Yeah, ouch. So we opted to hit the barrels first, which would eliminate the +1 damage modifiers, as well as hit the projections. Scholar had three flesh to irons at the ready, so it was actually less damage this way in the long run. Since the wagons took out all of the projections for us, would that mean X would be reduced to (0 projections +1 = 1)? Or does it stay the number it was at before the projections were destroyed?</span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:01.269Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
